content='```yaml\n---\n- name: Check if Helm binary exists\n  stat:\n    path: /usr/local/bin/helm\n  register: helm_check\n\n- name: Check Helm version\n  command: helm version --short\n  register: helm_existing_version\n  when: helm_check.stat.exists\n\n- name: Download helm\n  unarchive:\n    src: "https://get.helm.sh/helm-v{{ helm_version }}-linux-amd64.tar.gz"\n    dest: /tmp\n    remote_src: yes\n  register: helm_download\n  when: \n    - not helm_check.stat.exists\n    - helm_existing_version.stdout is not defined\n    - helm_existing_version.stdout != "v{{ helm_version }}"\n\n- name: Copy helm binary into place\n  copy:\n    src: "/tmp/linux-amd64/helm"\n    dest: /usr/local/bin/helm\n    mode: \'0755\'\n  become: yes\n  when: helm_download is changed\n```\n\nThis playbook is structured to be included in an Ansible Role under the `tasks/` directory. It starts with a check for the existence of the Helm binary, then checks the current Helm version. If Helm is not installed or the version does not match the desired version, it downloads Helm and copies the binary to the appropriate location with elevated privileges if necessary.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'phi4:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-20T07:06:03.560730589Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 3694204345, 'load_duration': 67869041, 'prompt_eval_count': 418, 'prompt_eval_duration': 26847844, 'eval_count': 280, 'eval_duration': 3598346131, 'model_name': 'phi4:14b'} id='run--18e5019c-fb10-43b1-b23e-3a1a75ef7816-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 418, 'output_tokens': 280, 'total_tokens': 698}
