e: Copy generated private SSH key for user\n  copy:\n    src: "/home/{{ user_name }}/.ssh/id_rsa"\n    dest: "{{ home_dir }}/.ssh/id_rsa"\n    owner: "{{ user_name }}"\n    mode: \'0600\'\n\n- name: Check users password valid time for user\n  shell: "chage -l {{ user_name }}"\n  register: password_validity\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: Set users password valid time for user\n  user:\n    name: "{{ user_name }}"\n    password_expire_min: "{{ password_min_days | default(7) }}"\n    password_expire_max: "{{ password_max_days | default(90) }}"\n\n- name: Place private key file for user\n  copy:\n    src: "/home/{{ user_name }}/.ssh/id_rsa"\n    dest: "{{ home_dir }}/.ssh/id_rsa"\n    owner: "{{ user_name }}"\n    mode: \'0600\'\n```\n\nIn this corrected playbook, I\'ve addressed the line length issues by breaking down the longer lines into multiple lines while adhering to YAML syntax. The lines that were too long were those containing the `args` for the `shell` module and the `validate` argument within the `copy` module task. Each of these lines has been split appropriately to ensure compliance with the specified line length limit of 80 characters.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'phi4:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-20T07:27:05.898176967Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 11348410805, 'load_duration': 77427121, 'prompt_eval_count': 1546, 'prompt_eval_duration': 495954538, 'eval_count': 816, 'eval_duration': 10773604629, 'model_name': 'phi4:14b'} id='run--8bd67155-ae0d-457c-920b-406b48aca447-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1546, 'output_tokens': 816, 'total_tokens': 2362}
